This plugin reuses ideas and, in places, code structure from two MIT-licensed
Obsidian plugins. Their notices are preserved below as required.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
obsidian-cursor-history — https://github.com/AbdelrahmanHafez/obsidian-cursor-history
Copyright (c) 2026 Abdelrahman Hafez

Derived work in this repository:
  - the "one global stack of cursor positions, browser-style back/forward"
    model and the `record` / `goBack` / `goForward` shape of the history
  - the line-distance heuristic that decides whether a cursor movement is a
    new history stop (`src/location.ts`)
  - the CodeMirror user-event classification used to spot deliberate jumps
    (`src/editor-jumps.ts`)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
obsidian-in-file-nav-history — https://github.com/beaurancourt/obsidian-in-file-nav-history
Copyright (c) 2026 Beau Rancourt

Derived work in this repository:
  - the idea of arming a "navigation intent" from a DOM click on an internal
    link or outline row, so that same-file heading jumps are detected in
    reading mode as well as in the editor (`src/main.ts`)
